    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **275 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city title-casing / spelling-reuse behavior for owner creation.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerFieldNormalizer.java`** \u2014 added a `titleCase(String)` helper that strips/collapses whitespace and upper-cases the first letter of each word with the rest lower-cased (e.g. `\"riverdale\"` \u2192 `\"Riverdale\"`). It reuses the existing `normalize(...)` method as the case-/whitespace-insensitive comparison key.\n\n2. **`NormalizeOwnerCity.java`** (new function class) \u2014 the pipeline step. It looks through existing owners: if one already lives in the same city (matched via `normalize`, i.e. case- and whitespace-insensitive), the new owner adopts that owner's *exact* stored city spelling; otherwise the city is title-cased.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired a `normalizeCity` step between `build` and `rejectDuplicate`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps, so it mutates the built `Owner` in place before it's saved and returned.\n\nThe behavior matches the spec and the `Cp12Tests`: a lowercase `\"riverdale5\"` is stored/returned as `\"Riverdale5\"`, and a second owner posting `\"GREENVALE5\"` reuses the first owner's `\"Greenvale5\"` spelling. Existing city-dependent behavior (Cp10 `customerCode`, which matches/formats case-insensitively) is unaffected.",
